                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "JGKK1",
                      "name": "cmp/ChatWorkspaceHub",
                      "context": "ChatWorkspaceHub (@pstdio/ui chat-ui, packages/ui/src/components/chat-ui/components/workspace-hub.tsx). The hub IS the composer frame: it wraps the session ChatInput so the session reads as living inside the workspace. Replaces the old 'N files changed … Review changes' toolbar.\n\nHeader = workspace identity (GitBranch + workspaceTitle, falling back to workspaceShorthand) + one variable slot + an icon-only open action (ArrowUpRight) that opens the workspace resource. The identity is always present; only the slot changes: DiffBubble counts when additions/deletions > 0, otherwise hidden; setup status (loader / AlertTriangle) while the workspace is being created or has failed, where the open action dims.\n\nContainment depends on the border hierarchy: the shell owns the visible border (ds-border) and the nested input recedes to ds-border-subtle. Do not invert this — the previous design had a subtle shell around a stronger input, which made the hub read as a toolbar floating above the composer instead of a frame around it. Radii are concentric: shell 8, padding 4, input 4. Header padding-left 8 + input padding 8 aligns the workspace name to the prompt text.\n\nThe open action is icon-only, so it needs a tooltip and aria-label ('Open workspace') in code.",
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "fill": "$ds-bg-subtle",
                      "cornerRadius": 4,
                      "stroke": "$ds-border",
                      "strokeWidth": 1,
