            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "B2H8jV",
              "name": "Kanban renderer",
              "context": "The collection renderer, drawn as a kanban. One renderer draws a whole resource set in two displays — a detailed list (tree: groups collapse, rows indent, attributes ride right as chips) and a kanban board (groups become columns, rows become draggable cards). Display is a setting on the renderer, not a mode of the workbench.\n\nTwo parts: a header (cmp/CollectionViewBar) naming the saved views and holding Search and the Filter, Sort, and Display menus, and the body, which is the display. A view is a NAME over its filter, sorts, and display, so switching a tab can change which resources are present, their order, and whether they are rows or cards. The criteria row lists the sort and every filter clause whenever the view has one, saved or not. Unsaved changes mark the tab and add Reset / Save.\n\nFull spec and both displays: the 'Kanban Renderer · Component' frame.",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 865,
              "fill": "$ds-bg-subtle",
              "cornerRadius": 12,
