        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "o0Mi1",
          "name": "F09 · Panel menu states · wide",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iddtz",
              "name": "Section Label",
              "fill": "$annotation",
              "content": "F09 · WIDE PANEL MENU STATES",
              "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 1.2
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "NDmPK",
              "name": "Section Note",
              "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
              "content": "Applies independently to Main, Secondary, and Side Panel. Dragging a divider closes an attached menu. Reopening attaches immediately when the panel is wider than 580px and the menu and minimum content widths fit; otherwise it floats.",
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "p9R6Y",
              "name": "F09 · Attached, closed, and dropdown menu anatomy",
              "context": "Panel menus default to 280px when attached. Collapsed menu openers use directional panel-left-open and panel-right-open icons rather than the active widget's content icon.",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$ds-bg-subtle",
              "cornerRadius": 12,
              "stroke": "$ds-border",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "strokeAlignment": "inner",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "padding": 20,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "do09O",
                  "name": "T",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg",
                  "content": "Panel anatomy",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "dSdDY",
                  "name": "D",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "Tabs and the + sit on the left of the strip. Attached panel menus default to 280px and have no internal header or close action; they collapse by dragging the divider closed. Closed menus use directional panel-open icons. Opening attaches directly when the panel is wider than 580px and minimum menu widths, dividers, and content fit. Narrower panels and insufficient horizontal space produce a floating menu.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "L5Ul0",
                  "name": "N",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-subtle",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "The menus belong to the panel, not the slot — bubblify the session into a floating panel and Context files goes with it, icon and all. This is also the reason the sidenav needs a resource region: navigating a workspace's children is not a panel action, so no panel menu can own it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
